ot need the same tattoo scale. A heavily tattooed person and first-time tattoo wearer may require completely different placement decisions. One person may want visible placement. The other may want private placement. DESIGN FOR TWO INDIVIDUAL HUMAN BODIES. PEOPLE VARIATION Across the complete collection naturally rotate: Guy and girl Girl and girl Guy and guy Also include: Friends Partners Brothers Sisters Siblings Mother and adult daughter Father and adult son Mother and adult son Father and adult daughter Grandparent and adult grandchild Chosen family Vary naturally: Skin tone Age within the adult range Body build Height Existing tattoo coverage Fashion Presentation Do not make the two people look like matching models. THE ARTWORK CONNECTS THEM. PRESENTATION FORMAT Generate ONE finished presentation image for every matching concept. LEFT SIDE: Show BOTH tattoo artworks cleanly on a neutral background. If they are identical: Show the artwork clearly enough to establish that both people receive the same design. If mirrored: Show both mirrored pieces. If complementary: Show both complete artworks beside one another. If split: Show both halves positioned so the viewer understands the completed artwork. If different scale: Show both versions at their intended relative sizes. If the designs create a third image: Show the relationship clearly. RIGHT SIDE: SHOW TWO REAL PEOPLE. Both people must be visible simultaneously. Person A wears Tattoo A on Person As specified body placement. Person B wears Tattoo B on Person Bs specified body placement. The tattoos must match the LEFT artwork exactly. Do not invent different tattoo designs for the body panel. Do not automatically put both tattoos on forearms. Do not automatically use the same body part. Respect the specific Person A and Person B placements. CONNECTING TATTOO PRESENTATION When the artwork physically connects, position the two people so the viewer can immediately understand the interaction. Examples: Two wrists beside one another Two forearms touching Two shoulders meeting Two calves aligned Two hands approaching Two backs beside one another The connection must actually work geometrically. Do not fake a connection that would be impossible on real bodies. INDEPENDENT MATCHING PRESENTATION When the tattoos do NOT physically connect, allow the two people to stand naturally. They do not need to touch. The viewer simply needs to see both tattoos clearly enough to understand their relationship. One tattoo may be: On a finger while the other is: On a wrist. One may be: Behind an ear while the other is: On an arm. One may be: On a thigh while the other is: On a shoulder. THAT IS INTENTIONAL'
